OpenWings patch 0022: Continue with ChatGPT (OpenAI's official sign-in)

ChatGPT Plus and Pro plans can power OpenWings through OpenAI's own Sign in
with ChatGPT for open-source apps (developers.openai.com/siwc), written from
OpenAI's documentation. It replaces, for anyone who uses it, the ChatGPT
Subscription provider that poses as OpenAI's Codex app (off since 0021).
The flow, storage and rules live in wings/chatgpt_plan.py and
wings/chatgpt_routes.py; this patch wires them into upstream:

  * src/llm_core.py: provider "chatgpt-plan" for exactly
    https://api.openai.com/v1/responses. Requests carry store:false and
    stream:true, the whole history in input, system text as instructions
    and none of the unsupported fields (no temperature, no
    max_output_tokens). Only response.completed counts as a finished
    answer; plan errors keep their status, code and request id, point to
    ChatGPT usage settings when a limit is reached, and never fall back to
    another way of paying. The synchronous call collects the stream.
  * src/endpoint_resolver.py: that URL stays whole (it is base and route at
    once), costs no per-token spend, gets OpenWings' own headers, and its
    token comes from wings.chatgpt_plan, which answers only the person who
    signed in (admins included are refused) and refreshes near expiry.
  * routes/model_routes.py: the endpoint is visible only to its owner, its
    models are OpenAI's listed catalog with OpenAI's display names (never
    probed with a chat request), and deleting it signs out (revocation at
    OpenAI). The picker cache is cleared after a sign-in or sign-out.
  * src/chatgpt_subscription.py, core/session_manager.py,
    routes/chat_helpers.py, routes/session_routes.py: like the subscription
    route, the short-lived token is resolved per request and never stored
    with a chat (uses_session_token).
  * static/js/wings-connect.js, static/index.html: "Use your ChatGPT plan"
    with a "Continue with ChatGPT" button (OpenAI's approved logo) in the
    first-run panel and Settings > Add Models; the one-time "You're using
    your ChatGPT plan" note; "Using ChatGPT plan · Manage usage" beside the
    model picker; sign out, use a different account, and when OpenWings is
    not on 127.0.0.1, the way to get there: the same computer, an SSH
    tunnel, or OpenAI's self-hosted steps (move the sign-in over SSH).
    The same file also carries the review fixes to 0021's Connect panels
    (they touch the same lines): the first-run panel stays until some
    endpoint has models, uses the height between the top bar and the
    message box (only what does not fit scrolls, with a fade and a "More
    below" cue), stacks on phones, and never covers a chat once one
    starts; a pasted key is kept only when the provider answers with
    models, and failures say what to do; links take each look's accent;
    OpenRouter, keys and app cards say that everyone on this OpenWings
    can use them; app cards show Waiting for sign-in at once, Could not
    connect with the reason, and a cancelled sign-in; a member sees whom
    to ask while there is no AI.

